-- examples/checks/agg-budget-data.rofl — THE BUDGET'S DATASET, shared by the
-- agg_<kind>_budget worlds (docs/aggregates.md, "Holes, as built"). A chain
-- of 40 nodes and its closure: the budget of each world cuts the evaluation
-- while the closure is still being derived, so every aggregate over it reads
-- a relation that never closed. A cut is a hole on the world,
-- hole($adhoc, budget_exhausted), and an aggregate over what was derived
-- before it is no answer: never a smaller count, a partial sum, the best of
-- what arrived, the median of a group cut short, or an empty group's 0. The
-- wall stops the rules of the world, so each world's file says, as lines of
-- the state (scripts/goldens.ts), which rows the cut state must hold and
-- must not.
edb(ab_e).
edb(ab_node).
ab_e(n0, n1, 1).
ab_e(n1, n2, 2).
ab_e(n2, n3, 3).
ab_e(n3, n4, 4).
ab_e(n4, n5, 5).
ab_e(n5, n6, 6).
ab_e(n6, n7, 7).
ab_e(n7, n8, 8).
ab_e(n8, n9, 9).
ab_e(n9, n10, 10).
ab_e(n10, n11, 11).
ab_e(n11, n12, 12).
